## (Genasis Overlay) Plane / Mattermost protocol

> Managed by `genasis`. Do not hand-edit between the GENASIS:BEGIN and
> GENASIS:END markers — `genasis upgrade` will detect the tamper and refuse
> to overwrite your changes. Make protocol changes by editing
> `crates/genasis-templates/templates/agent-overlays/frontend.patch.md.tera`
> in the framework repo.

- **My Plane PAT**: `${PLANE_TOKEN_FRONTEND}` (falls back to `PLANE_API_KEY` only during initial bootstrap).
- **My Mattermost bot**: `${MM_TOKEN_FRONTEND}`.
- **My Plane user UUID**: `${PLANE_USER_ID_FRONTEND}` — issues with this UUID in `assignees` are mine.
- **My channel**: `#scrum-{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` on `{{ mm_url | default(value="<mattermost-url>") }}`.

### What I own
- `src/components/**`, `src/app/**`, `src/styles/**`, `src/lib/client/**`.
- Any Plane issue whose `assignees` contains `${PLANE_USER_ID_FRONTEND}`.

### Lifecycle (assignee-primary)
1. **Todo → In Progress** — create `feat/{seq}-{slug}` branch, `PATCH` issue
   state with my PAT, reply on the Mattermost thread that hosted the human
   request.
2. **In Progress → In Review** — push the branch, open a PR, ensure
   `unit: pass` and `integration: pass` are stated in the PR body, mention
   `@qa.{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` on the issue thread.
3. **In Review → Done** — only after QA ✅. Merge with
   `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`, sync `main`, transition state to
   Done with my PAT, post the final summary in the issue thread.

### Design system
- Single source of truth: [`docs/design-system.md`](docs/design-system.md).
- Reference it before introducing tokens, colours, spacing, typography.
- Hot-swap is orchestrated by `genasis design swap` — wait for the
  `🚨 DESIGN CHANGE` Mattermost root before resuming UI work.

### Database
- Read-only inspection: `genasis db query "SELECT ..."` (DDL/DML rejected by
  the SQL guard).
- Schema change: open a PR that touches `db/schema/**`; CI runs
  `genasis db diff` and routes the review through `architect` and
  `database-reviewer`.

### Token economics
- RTK is wrapped onto shell tool calls if it is installed.
- Tool results larger than `[token_economics] trim_threshold_kb` (default
  32 KB) are auto-trimmed by the `post-tool-trim.sh` hook.

### Forbidden
- Direct `commit`/`push` to `main` — branch protection rejects it; if the
  hook ever silences, this fence is the second guardrail.
- Bypassing QA — never merge without an `@qa` ✅ on the issue thread.

> Refer to `GENASIS.md` (project root, imported via `CLAUDE.md @import`) for
> the full lifecycle state machine and DoD checklist.
